        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Rectangular piece; one full width plus another half, seamed. Natural colored cotton warp and weft. Printed in blue with roller-print. Pattern shows groups of figures dancing, drinking and conversing under palm trees. On end of cask at right edge of textile initials JMandS; under seated couple, right center, plate inscribed Jn. Marshall and Sons. Selvedges complete on larger piece; one selvedge on smaller piece. Cotton browned, a number of holes."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/699ce5c1-037b-3e40-b672-966c138a386b> ;
